#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.10.pod:109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" - The 'HACKING' file is obsolete.  The contents have been moved into\n"
"   a section of the guestfs(3) manual page.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" - Файл 'HACKING' устарел. Его содержимое перемещено в раздел\n"
"   страницы руководства guestfs(3).\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.10.pod:112
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" - libguestfs-test-tool simplified.  It no longer needs the static\n"
"   binary or tries to construct an ISO.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" - libguestfs-test-tool упрощен. Он больше не требует статического\n"
"   бинарного файла и не пытается создать ISO.\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.10.pod:115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" - rpcgen-generated files are compiled with -fno-strict-aliasing\n"
"   which should be safer (thanks Matt Booth).\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" - Файлы, сгенерированные rpcgen, компилируются с -fno-strict-aliasing,\n"
"   что должно быть безопаснее (спасибо Matt Booth).\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.10.pod:118
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" - virt-resize was rewritten in OCaml.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" - virt-resize был переписан на OCaml.\n"
"\n"

#. type: verbatim
#: docs/guestfs-release-notes-1.10.pod:120
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" - guestfish and other tools tested with valgrind; some memory leaks\n"
"   were fixed.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
" - guestfish и другие инструменты протестированы с valgrind; некоторые\n"
"   утечки памяти исправлены.\n"
"\n"

